      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eI looked into the issue that you reported. In every case that IBulkCursor#close took too long to return, the root cause was that the call to close was issued shortly before the CPUs were suspended or the client app was frozen, and the result was delivered after resuming from suspend/freeze, thus causing a timeout in terms of wall time. This is unfortunately kind of inevitable in apps that rely on finalizers to do significant work\n\nNo, this is a direct result of the freezer pretending that it is invisible to applications, and a known issue. https://b.corp.google.com/issues/118997212\n\nPlease fix this so that applications can have useful timeouts in the presence of the freezer. Would it be so painful to have a freezer-aware clock with which to measure timeouts?",
